        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "承認後の fresh review finding を通常レーンで user 裁定なしに適用可能とする決定は、`pre-track-adr-authoring.md` の Phase 0 手順3（承認済み文面への意味変更が必要な finding は自己解決せず user 裁定へ戻す）および入力 ADR の意味は user に属するという既存方針と矛盾する。Consequences でも承認済み文面の意味変更が guardian 判定だけで採用されうることを認めており、Phase 0 の裁定境界を実質的に弱めている。承認後に通常レーンへ戻せるのは非意味的修正または決定保存的な修正に限定し、意味変更は従来どおり user 裁定または delta 候補へ送る必要がある。",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "knowledge/adr/2026-07-25-0716-phase0-post-approval-reconvergence-lane.md",
              "line": 35,
              "category": "inconsistent decisions within the same ADR"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:dd9cddb5593283b08bdbbd536f9d3d5832f174989aa4a7b9b1ea82daf66f615e",
          "at": "2026-07-25T08:13:53Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "D1 permits meaning-changing edits to an already user-approved ADR to be adopted through guardian review without renewed user adjudication. This contradicts the existing Phase 0 boundary and ADR decision-freeze policy: only non-semantic or decision-preserving edits may remain in the in-place lane; edits that alter the effective decision must be restored and sent to user adjudication (or a delta/hearing path). The Negative consequence explicitly confirms this unsafe behavior.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "knowledge/adr/2026-07-25-0716-phase0-post-approval-reconvergence-lane.md",
              "line": 45,
              "category": "inconsistent decisions"
            }
          ],
